From b7e94aa4d20c6ddb72573a6b84d898ed342010d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andy1210 <andy1210@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 19:26:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 104/147] ASoC: qdsp6: q6voice-dai: Add VoiceMMode2 and the
 LPASS codec DMA ports

Newer modem firmware runs a call of the first subscription on the
VoiceMMode1 voice session and one of the second (dual SIM) on
VoiceMMode2. Add the VoiceMMode2 front end next to VoiceMMode1.

SoCs with the LPASS codec macros (SM8250 and later) have their speakers,
earpiece and microphones on the codec DMA ports, not on MI2S. Let every
voice front end take its uplink from the VA and TX codec DMA ports and
play its downlink into WSA_CODEC_DMA_RX_0/1 and RX_CODEC_DMA_RX_0,
through the same "<FE> Capture Mixer" and "<PORT> Voice Mixer" switches
the MI2S ports use. The mixer tables are generated from one list per
direction, so a front end can no longer miss a port the others have.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
